    "durationMs": 188156,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Structure** — Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21 in `/workspace`:\n- `pom.xml` — added `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`, Flyway (+ PostgreSQL module), and the PostgreSQL driver\n- `bench.app` package: `Link` entity, `LinkRepository` (Spring Data JPA with an atomic `clicks + 1` update query), `LinkService`, `LinkController`, DTO records, and `ApiExceptionHandler` mapping errors to JSON `{\"error\": ...}`\n- `DatabaseUrlEnvironmentPostProcessor` — parses the `DATABASE_URL` env var (`postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db`) into `spring.datasource.*` properties, so no credentials are hard-coded\n- `V1__init.sql` Flyway migration (links table with unique code, text url, click counter, timestamps), applied at startup before serving\n- `start.sh` (executable, runs the prebuilt jar from any cwd) and a README start section\n\n**Verified end-to-end against the spec:**\n- POST `/links` → 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged; auto-generated 8-char codes; explicit `code: null` treated as omitted\n- Duplicate custom code → 409; malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url` (ftp, relative, no host), and invalid codes → 422; uppercase `HTTP://` schemes accepted per RFC 3986 case-insensitivity (fixed after testing caught this)\n- GET `/links/{code}` → 200 / 404; GET `/links` → ascending creation order with `total`\n- GET `/r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` exactly equal to the stored URL; two redirects yielded `clicks: 2` (exactly one increment each)\n- Restarted the server: all links and click counts survived; Flyway reported \"schema up to date\" on re-run\n- Database left clean (my test rows deleted), server stopped, port 8000 free for the harness"
  }
